# Splash contract

Only edit these files when the user asked to change the splash.

- Logo box is **112px**, `background-image` (not `<img>`), `transform: none`
- Position: `top: calc(50% - 14vh - 56px); left: calc(50% - 56px)` — same formula as generated iOS PNGs
- Sequence: logo first, tagline fades in after ~800ms; tagline is `position: absolute` so the logo does not move
- `#vibeup-boot-splash` stays outside `AppProviders`; `SplashScreen` returns `null`
- Standalone PWA must **not** skip the HTML splash (iOS always shows a native splash first)
- `apple-touch-startup-image`: every link needs a media query; include dark + landscape variants
- Status bar: `black-translucent` so native PNG and HTML share one coordinate space
- `color-scheme` must be `only dark` (html/body/meta/boot CSS) so iOS Light Mode does not paint a white WKWebView canvas between the native launch image and the HTML splash
- Never inline the full app CSS into `<head>` (`experimental.inlineCss`); it delays `<body>` past the iOS launch-image handoff
